WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.030
[Snake Beasts hiss]

3
00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.140
[KANJURO]
What in the world is going on?

4
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.290
<b>Kin'emon's Clever Ruse</b>

5
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:38.160
[KANJURO]
How did Luffy's crew find us?

6
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.350
How did Luffy's crew find us?

7
00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.830
And Law is here as well!

8
00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.370
I was told that he
had been apprehended!

9
00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.380
[gasps]
You unhand me
this instant, Kanjuro!

10
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.130
[Kanjuro gasps]
I dutifully reported everything

11
00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.170
to Lord Orochi just like always!

12
00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.620
What could have gone awry?

13
00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:55.160
It can't be.

14
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.960
Did Lord Orochi not arrange
any countermeasures for this?

15
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.010
Do you really think
a regular old bomb

16
00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.970
would take down
a ship like ours?

17
00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:03.840
Not a chance in hell, bro!

18
00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.140
[All gasp]

19
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.680
[FRANKY]
The Sunny can
cross a thousand seas!

20
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.060
It's made of wood
from the Tree of Adam!

21
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.600
It won't go down that easy!

22
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.940
You got anything else?

23
00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.980
'Cause those weak-ass bombs
ain't gonna cut it!

24
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.400
So the sabotage wasn't enough?

25
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.110
[FRANKY]
Those sneaky scumbags couldn't

26
00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.450
put a scratch on our ship!

27
00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:28.120
Uh, the sails are
another story, though.

28
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.410
[gasps]

29
00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.830
Sorry we're late, Kin'emon!

30
00:02:32.830 --> 00:02:35.790
We had to patch up the sails
and that took a little while!

31
00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.960
Quite all right!
Though it gave me a scare!

32
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.130
[LUFFY]
Hey, Kin!

33
00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:42.970
Where is everybody?

34
00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.760
I thought you were
bringing backup!

35
00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.640
I guess our original plans
kinda changed, huh?

36
00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.850
Is it okay if we smash those
battleships to pieces then?

37
00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:52.230
Yes, what happened?

38
00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:53.810
I was under the impression
we would have

39
00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.730
lots of reinforcements here.

40
00:02:55.730 --> 00:03:00.610
Yeah! Where are the 3,500 people
from the Labor Camp?

41
00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.740
Indeed. What's the status?

42
00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.450
Where are the yakuza
who were supposed to be

43
00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.570
coming from all over
the country?

44
00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.420
Weren't there about
200 or so of them?

45
00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.170
Something is not adding up.

46
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.130
Dogstorm had 200 Musketeers
at Itachi Port.

47
00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.920
And then the Atamayama
Thieves Brigade had 280!

48
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.090
Yeah, and where are all
the ships we repaired?

49
00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.550
There were dozens of them,
what happened?

50
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.600
And what about that supply
of swords and spears

51
00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.430
that was coming in from Ringo?

52
00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.730
Without weapons for our troops,
we're screwed!

53
00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.810
[NAMI]
Hey, Kin'emon!
Know anything about this?

54
00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.290
[KIN'EMON]
I confess.
A substantial misstep was made.

55
00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:49.700
[gasps]

56
00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:50.720
[KIN'EMON]
My deepest apologies, Sir Luffy!

57
00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.040
[KIN'EMON]
My deepest
apologies, Sir Luffy!

58
00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.060
Regrettably,
the entire plan was leaked!

59
00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:00.120
I wish I could tell you
where the others are,

60
00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.080
but I know nothing at all!

61
00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.170
So that's the reason
why nobody's here!

62
00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.420
We should think about
retreating, maybe?

63
00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:06.660
[CARROT]
No way! That's messed up!

64
00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.230
No way! That's messed up!

65
00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.440
We don't know jack
about what's going on!

66
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.580
In fact, we thought we sunk your
ship until just a second ago.

67
00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.290
But we did sink all of
the ships at the dock.

68
00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.720
You should have seen
the port last night!

69
00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.380
The shogun was thorough.

70
00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.970
He had us bomb
the major bridges, too.

71
00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:24.570
Now there's no passage
between the regions.

72
00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:24.950
now?

73
00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.850
You get it, right? [laughs]

74
00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:33.270
There's not a chance in hell
anyone's coming to help you!

75
00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:35.270
[BIRD GIFTER A]
Even if they
made it to the port,

76
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.610
no one's gonna be reaching
Onigashima without a boat!

77
00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.970
[Shishilian grunts]

78
00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:40.490
And this was your last chance!

79
00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:42.700
The only day the raid
might succeed!

80
00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.580
[BUTTERFLY GIFTER A]
And by
the way, I heard we're going to

81
00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.910
start killing all the rebels
we rounded up tomorrow!

82
00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:52.580
[Gifters laughing]

83
00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:49.640
I almost forgot! There's one
last thing we need to tell you!

84
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:50.860
I almost forgot!

85
00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.900
There's one last thing
we need to tell you!

86
00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:53.440
[BIRD GIFTER A]
Sorry about that.

87
00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.400
[BIRD GIFTER A]
Sorry about
that, figured there's only

88
00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.780
Figured there's only so much
bad news you can take!

89
00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:57.650
so much bad news you can take!

90
00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.070
Bad news, you say?

91
00:04:59.070 --> 00:04:59.820
[BIRD GIFTER A]
That banquet we're having

92
00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:00.200
[BUTTERFLY GIFTER A]
That banquet we're having

93
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.160
isn't just for
the Fire Festival,

94
00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.830
it's much bigger than that!

95
00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.460
It's a once-in-a-lifetime
celebration!

96
00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.750
Because the Beast Pirates
and the Big Mom Pirates

97
00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:12.040
are forming the
ultimate alliance!

98
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.010
You have got to be shitting me.

99
00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:17.610
Two Emperors teaming up?

100
00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:19.700
We're unstoppable
with both Commander Kaido

101
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:22.970
[Both grunt]

102
00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:21.360
and Big Mom on our side!

103
00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:24.160
No matter who you recruit,
you got nothing on us!

104
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:27.000
The Worst Generation?
Yeah, I'll say!

105
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.790
Sink 'em and get this
over with already!

106
00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.960
Now, get ready to fire!

107
00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.180
Man, you're really
full of yourselves, huh?

108
00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:46.260
Well, I'm sick of it!
Stand back, you guys!

109
00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:49.310
You stand back!
Take your own dumb advice.

110
00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.850
I got this, Traffy.

111
00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.190
Make yourself useful
and stay out of it!

112
00:05:53.190 --> 00:05:54.690
I said no, back off!

113
00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:58.650
All right, ladies,
stop your bickering. I got this.

114
00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.860
Dammit, Jaggy! Not you, too!

115
00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.820
[KID]
Pipe down! You're annoying!

116
00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:05.030
Neither of you better
get in my way!

117
00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.620
Watch me! I was here first!

118
00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:09.080
Get back here!

119
00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:11.120
[LUFFY]
I said I got this!

120
00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.290
Oh, like hell you do!

121
00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:17.000
[Luffy, Kid yell]

122
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.420
[Luffy, Kid gasp]

123
00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.550
You back off!

124
00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.630
Go away!

125
00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.260
Room's even more effective
in the rain.

126
00:06:23.260 --> 00:06:25.180
No fair! Your power's too cool!

127
00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.970
Why do you gotta
go and rub it in?

128
00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.060
Suck it up.

129
00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:30.140
You don't need to be
a damn showoff!

130
00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.940
Oh, the kettle has an opinion.

131
00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:33.270
You're both dumb!

132
00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:35.400
I can wrap this up
in one shot, you know!

133
00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:36.940
Would you shut up?

134
00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.980
Also, I can do the same damn
thing in half the time as you!

135
00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:41.400
We're wasting time!

136
00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:43.530
I'm going in,
and you can't stop me.

137
00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.160
You got that, losers?

138
00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.700
[LUFFY, KID]
– Losers?
– Losers?

139
00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:48.450
[KID]
Now I'll kick your ass first!

140
00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:50.370
[LUFFY]
Good! 'Cuz I'll
handle these guys!

141
00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:51.750
[LAW]
You're ridiculous.

142
00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.210
Hey! You three!

143
00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:55.500
Don't go thinking that
you'll leave here alive!

144
00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.460
Shut up! You're beneath me!

145
00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:59.500
[LAW]
You shut up.
I'll take care of 'em.

146
00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.420
Oh yeah? It's on now!

147
00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:06.970
[Kid, Luffy grunt]

148
00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.760
Room!

149
00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:20.960
[BEAST PIRATE B]
Boss?

150
00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:42.840
[grunts]
Bounce-Man!

151
00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.520
Punk Vise!

152
00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.650
Injection Shot!

153
00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:23.340
[yells]

154
00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:35.980
[laughs]

155
00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:39.420
See what I did there?
Who's the loser now, loser?

156
00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:42.040
Let me make one thing
perfectly clear.

157
00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:44.670
I'm the one who
sank that last ship.

158
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.300
I sank that thing!
It was all me!

159
00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.840
Get outta here with that!

160
00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:50.630
You're taking credit
for my work!

161
00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:53.890
[yells]

162
00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.050
[chuckles]

163
00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.930
[BEAST PIRATE K]
That's the
Kyoshiro Family's ship!

164
00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:03.060
Perfect timing, Kyoshiro.
We had nothing to fear!

165
00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:07.980
Perfect timing, Kyoshiro!
We had nothing to fear!

166
00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.070
Seems you're in
quite a bit of trouble.

167
00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:12.160
We could really use some help!

168
00:09:12.160 --> 00:09:13.910
The shogun ordered
for them to be sunk

169
00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:15.660
to the bottom of the sea, but...

170
00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:15.710
But

171
00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.120
You don't say.

172
00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.380
Orders to sink the enemy, huh?

173
00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:21.920
Allow me.

174
00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:26.260
[All chattering]

175
00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.980
Of course!

176
00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.370
I've no desire to sink you.

177
00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:38.160
So I simply disabled the cannons

178
00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.030
you had aimed at
the samurai's vessel.

179
00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:42.960
I know him. We fought before.

180
00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.080
[SHUTENMARU]
Careful of this one!

181
00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:44.160
He's terrifying with a blade.

182
00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.050
[ZORO]
He's

183
00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.380
This man is one of
the shogun's lapdogs.

184
00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:52.050
He's the yakuza boss who
took over after Hyogoro.

185
00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.430
Greetings to you,
Akazaya samurai!

186
00:09:57.430 --> 00:10:01.060
I'm the reputable gangster
who runs the Flower Capital!

187
00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:04.060
The people there know me
as Napping Kyoshiro!

188
00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:04.180
My family's made up of 200 men!

189
00:10:04.180 --> 00:10:06.270
[DENJIRO]
My family's made up of 200 men!

190
00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:06.430
Our swords are at your
disposal for the raid!

191
00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:09.650
Our swords are your
disposal for the raid!

192
00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.070
[All gasp]

193
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:11.110
that you?

194
00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:12.440
[BEAST PIRATES]
They're doing what now?

195
00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.250
Are you joking, Boss?

196
00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.540
Explain yourself!

197
00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:16.170
What favor do you owe us?

198
00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.010
Do you not operate under Orochi?

199
00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.180
[DENJIRO]
My intent is to
pay back the immeasurable debt

200
00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.930
that I owe the Kozuki Clan.

201
00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:31.980
You have been in my thoughts,
Kin, for years.

202
00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:34.230
[gasps]
You know me?

203
00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:35.860
Do you recall when
the Mountain God

204
00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.570
charged into the capital
40 years ago?

205
00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.450
[roars]

206
00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.280
[DENJIRO]
The public
believed that the chaos

207
00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:46.280
was the result of
Lord Oden's antics.

208
00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:48.660
But they were wrong
in that assumption.

209
00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:52.160
It was, in fact, caused by
you and your ill-advised plan

210
00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.710
to get rich by selling
a young boar!

211
00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:59.280
[Mountain God roaring] [gasps]

212
00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.700
[KIN'EMON]
What? But only one man knows

213
00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.280
about what happened that day!

214
00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.180
[Townspeople scream]

215
00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.980
Why do you think everyone
calls it the Mountain God?

216
00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:09.540
What?

217
00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.250
It's all my fault!

218
00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:14.460
The capital's doomed
and it's my fault!

219
00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:17.130
[KIN'EMON]
No. Don't tell me.

220
00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:18.760
Is that you, Denjiro?

221
00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.790
– It can't be!
– It's really true?

222
00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:24.830
That's impossible!

223
00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.250
[chuckles]

224
00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:30.000
[DENJIRO]
I suppose you
wouldn't recognize me.

225
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:31.880
I wished to join you right away.

226
00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.760
However, I determined
it'd be wiser to

227
00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:37.090
appear to be your enemy,
just a bit longer.

228
00:11:34.830 --> 00:11:36.880
[both gasp]

229
00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:39.760
Imagine if I revealed who I was?

230
00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:41.640
The betrayer in your
midst would have

231
00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:46.310
relayed that to Orochi
and had me killed!

232
00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:47.520
Denjiro!

233
00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.650
Silence, you!

234
00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:52.480
[DENJIRO]
Instead, I retained
his trust until the end,

235
00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:54.990
and I liberated
the 1,000 samurai

236
00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:58.070
locked in the Rasetsu
Prison Quarters!

237
00:11:58.070 --> 00:11:59.370
There're more ships!

238
00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.920
[FRANKY]
Enemy reinforcements?

239
00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:06.420
[DENJIRO]
You can add
1,200 soldiers to the total!

240
00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:12.430
[Samurai yelling]

241
00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:13.680
We've been waiting for this day,

242
00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:16.180
and we're ready to fight
with all we've got!

243
00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:17.730
Since when is Boss Kyoshiro

244
00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.480
one of the damned
Akazaya Samurai?

245
00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:22.940
Go inform Onigashima
before it's too late!

246
00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:24.820
[Beast Pirate A gasps]
Yessir!

247
00:12:30.810 --> 00:12:33.270
It's really you!

248
00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:35.270
[DENJIRO]
Commendable work, Kin!

249
00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.940
I knew you were sharp,
but I must hand it to you!

250
00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:42.520
You understood Lord Yasuie's
message and adapted quickly!

251
00:12:42.520 --> 00:12:42.550
[KIN'EMON]
Two birds aflame
to represent time.

252
00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:44.900
Two birds aflame
to represent time.

253
00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:45.010
A habu viper to
indicate location.

254
00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:47.450
A habu viper
to indicate location.

255
00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:51.180
And a reversed crescent moon,
which signifies rebellion!

256
00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:54.810
"Twilight, the second hour
of the bird at Fire Festival.

257
00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:57.370
It shall take place
at Habu Port."

258
00:12:57.370 --> 00:13:01.210
The initial symbol did not
have those two lines.

259
00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:05.590
[DENJIRO]
That was the one
that Orochi got his hands on.

260
00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.010
[DENJIRO]
Before his death,
Lord Yasuie altered it

261
00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.800
and helped get word out!

262
00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:13.470
Obviously the newly added lines

263
00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:15.060
going through the
serpents stomachs

264
00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.640
instruct the reader to remove
the midsection of the word.

265
00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:23.530
<b>Habuminato</b>

266
00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.480
So without the letters
in the center,

267
00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:25.610
Habu Port, also called
"Habuminato," becomes "Hato"!

268
00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.990
<b>Hato</b>

269
00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.660
<b>(Hato)</b>

270
00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:26.620
<b>Wharf</b>

271
00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:31.070
[DENJIRO]
It means "wharf."
Lord Yasuie always did love

272
00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:35.330
the view of the maple tree
forest from there.

273
00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:38.210
– Huh?
– [Kanjuro gasps]

274
00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:40.080
[DENJIRO]
Even though it was
a simple message,

275
00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:43.670
you deliberately misinterpreted
it when you spoke.

276
00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.840
[DENJIRO]
Sensing there was
a spy was amongst your group,

277
00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:51.340
you pretended to direct
your associates elsewhere!

278
00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:54.850
But you knew they were wise
enough to discern the truth!

279
00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:55.090
At any rate, the point is
each of these ports

280
00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:57.430
At any rate, the point is,
each of these ports

281
00:13:57.430 --> 00:13:59.940
is associated with
a particular animal.

282
00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:01.400
And with a moment's
consideration,

283
00:13:59.940 --> 00:13:59.940
With a moment's consideration,

284
00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:04.520
the image of a lizard
will likely come to mind.

285
00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:09.150
Thus, Tokage port in Udon.

286
00:14:09.150 --> 00:14:13.700
Thinking back, that symbol
never did look like a lizard.

287
00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:15.080
I had no reason to question it

288
00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.540
because Master Kin
was so confident.

289
00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.540
[DENJIRO]
The unwitting spy passed along

290
00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:22.380
word of the false
rendezvous point to Orochi,

291
00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:25.540
just as you planned, Master Kin!

292
00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.300
[DENJIRO]
Such is the foolishness of a man

293
00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:30.970
who did as he pleased
for too long!

294
00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.640
Orochi misjudged the distance
between locations

295
00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.110
and waited until
last night to act.

296
00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:37.160
[DENJIRO]
By the time
they began their assault,

297
00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:40.120
all of your allied forces had
already crossed the bridges,

298
00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:42.540
and the ships you need
had left the port!

299
00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:46.330
The ones they sank were
those few left behind!

300
00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.750
So according to your plan,

301
00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:51.040
the 4,200 troops
concealed themselves!

302
00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:53.170
They laid in wait,
within the maple forest

303
00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:56.090
near the wharf at Habu Port!

304
00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:58.510
You mean they're still alive?

305
00:14:58.510 --> 00:15:05.560
[Samurai yelling]

306
00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:13.800
[Samurai yelling]

307
00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.550
It may be 20 years later,

308
00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:18.930
but I still remember
Lord Oden's legendary death!

309
00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:22.850
We've lived every day believing
the Kozuki Clan would return!

310
00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:26.600
Akazaya Nine!
Let us fight together!

311
00:15:26.600 --> 00:15:31.190
We are here to aid you!

312
00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:33.020
[DENJIRO]
The plan to raid Onigashima

313
00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:35.740
hasn't missed a single step!

314
00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:39.780
[DENJIRO]
Combine our 1,200
soldiers with your troops

315
00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:43.860
and you now stand
at 5,400 strong!

316
00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:48.080
To

317
00:15:48.080 --> 00:15:50.580
Onward! To the banquet!

318
00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:52.400
[Samurai yell]

319
00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:54.940
[laughs]
Would ya look at that!

320
00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.320
[Luffy chuckles]

321
00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.950
I don't really follow
what happened,

322
00:15:57.950 --> 00:15:59.990
but looks like
everything worked out!

323
00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:01.660
There's too many of them!

324
00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.660
Things aren't
looking good for us!

325
00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.750
Any news from Onigashima?

326
00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:07.210
Can't get ahold of them!

327
00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:10.970
I bet they're preoccupied
with the big party right now!

328
00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:14.600
[KANJURO]
So my efforts were
all for naught in the end?

329
00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:18.820
Damn you, Kin'emon!

330
00:16:20.050 --> 00:16:22.240
[DENJIRO]
Bravo! As expected,
you have risen to the occasion

331
00:16:22.240 --> 00:16:24.940
and proven to be
quite the capable leader!

332
00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:29.950
[Samurai cheering]

333
00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:31.370
[Kin'emon sighs]

334
00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:55.890
You-gara can be
honest with us, Kin'emon.

335
00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:57.760
No offense, but we've
known you long enough

336
00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:01.940
to know that a plan like this
is not within your skillset.

337
00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:04.900
Just admit you made a mistake,
and we won't be angry.

338
00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.270
Stop it.

339
00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:08.110
You thought
the message was "Tokage."

340
00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.400
You cannot fool me!

341
00:17:09.400 --> 00:17:10.570
I said stop it.

342
00:17:10.570 --> 00:17:12.780
At least the mistake
settled in our favor!

343
00:17:12.780 --> 00:17:14.910
What a happy accident.

344
00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.200
To be honest,
I fear that I might

345
00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.080
perish in the battle ahead.

346
00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.160
[All gasp]

347
00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.000
I did just use up
a whole lifetime's

348
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:27.380
worth of luck, after all.

349
00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.800
I can scarcely
disagree with that!

350
00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.260
[SAMURAI D]
Master Kin'emon!

351
00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.090
[SAMURAI E]
We'll follow you anywhere!

352
00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:34.800
[SHUTENMARU]
Though if you are lucky,

353
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:38.680
then we are lucky to have you
at our side in this battle!

354
00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:43.940
And even if you die out there,

355
00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:46.360
at the very least,
we will all die beside you!

356
00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:49.400
We served Lord Oden together,
and we'll avenge him together.

357
00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.110
We may have come from
different worlds,

358
00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:54.820
but we are comrades
in arms now, till the end!

359
00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:04.790
Such pleasantries
from scoundrels like you?

360
00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.080
Hardly comforting.

361
00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:09.000
[All chuckle]

362
00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.000
Hold up your sword
with pride, Kin!

363
00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.460
We shall claim victory
in the opening fight!

364
00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:19.050
[Samurai yell]

365
00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:21.810
Win or lose, I'm prepared!

366
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.330
We will avenge Lord Oden!

367
00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.670
The time is now!

368
00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.170
[Samurai yell]

369
00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:31.400
[SAMURAI G]
You have our full
support no matter the cost!

370
00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:37.460
[Samurai yelling]

371
00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:36.030
[chuckles]

372
00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:41.040
[KANJURO]
Never mind Kin'emon.
I must make haste to Onigashima!

373
00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:45.260
The role assigned to me by Lord
Orochi is still unfulfilled!

374
00:18:46.010 --> 00:18:48.180
There's one thing
I have left to do!

375
00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:49.640
[gasps]

376
00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:02.910
You won't take Lord Momonosuke!

377
00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:08.460
Kawamatsu! I am on my way!

378
00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.430
Stop it! You'll drown
if you jump into the sea!

379
00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:15.560
You would trample our dreams
and gut us with a smile?!

380
00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:18.520
You bastard!

381
00:19:18.520 --> 00:19:22.400
I admit, I do find pleasure
in this moment!

382
00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:25.820
Sabotage, duplicity, betrayal
with a surprise ending!

383
00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:29.570
What a complex role
I had the honor to play!

384
00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:32.450
And speaking of roles,
thank you all so much

385
00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:33.780
for playing the fool!

386
00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:36.790
[Kawamatsu gasps]

387
00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:38.290
Kanjuro!

388
00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:40.970
[Kanjuro chuckles]

389
00:19:41.580 --> 00:19:42.710
[Kawamatsu grunts]

390
00:19:44.340 --> 00:19:46.090
What better way to end the play

391
00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:49.380
than to stain the stage
with Kozuki blood?

392
00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:53.460
[gasps]

393
00:19:55.690 --> 00:19:57.360
Kawamatsu, help!

394
00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.660
[KAWAMATSU]
Lord Momonosuke!

395
00:19:59.660 --> 00:20:01.490
Don't you worry, Momonosuke.

396
00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:04.040
I'll let your sister
follow you into death.

397
00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.500
You hear that, Kawamatsu?

398
00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:08.420
I will find Hiyori
and slay her, too!

399
00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:12.130
You fools confirmed
she's alive, after all!

400
00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:16.300
Damn you, Kanjuro!

401
00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.970
That crane you painted
is flying immaculately!

402
00:20:18.970 --> 00:20:21.220
What of the monstrosities
you made us?

403
00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:23.260
They washed away with water!

404
00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.040
I thought you lacked talent!

405
00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:27.250
[Momonosuke cries]
It's too high!

406
00:20:27.250 --> 00:20:31.700
Someone please get me down from
here, please, I don't wanna die!

407
00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:33.920
[LUFFY]
Kanjuro? Momo?

408
00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:33.960
[Both gasp]

409
00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:35.750
Wait! Where are you going?

410
00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.630
This is the last
you'll ever see of me!

411
00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.420
[Momonosuke cries]

412
00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:42.670
[KANJURO]
This is only a fraction

413
00:20:42.670 --> 00:20:44.590
of Commander Kaido's army!

414
00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:48.260
You'll be dead before
you ever reach the shore!

415
00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:52.140
[cackles]

416
00:20:58.310 --> 00:20:59.980
Lord Momonosuke, no!

417
00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:02.290
You'll pay for betraying
the Akazaya Nine, Kanjuro!

418
00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:02.850
Kanjuro!

419
00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:04.690
Stay strong, Lord Momonosuke!

420
00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.020
This is terrible!

421
00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:07.200
[Samurai gasping]
- [Kanjuro cackles]
- [Momonosuke crying]

422
00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:09.830
Damn. So the whole plan
nearly fell apart

423
00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.790
'cause Kanjuro's been
feeding info to the enemy?

424
00:21:12.790 --> 00:21:14.080
So it would seem.

425
00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.920
We'd better save Momo, quick.

426
00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.920
[gasps]

427
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.340
On it!

428
00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.340
[Sanji grunts]

429
00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:25.880
Hey, Luffy!

430
00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:29.060
It turns out Kanjuro is
actually an enemy spy!

431
00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:31.810
He's taking Momo away right now!

432
00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.940
Huh?! Are you sure?

433
00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:39.520
No way! He fooled us all this
time and nobody had a clue?

434
00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.610
[LUFFY]
What a jerk!

435
00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.700
[yells]

436
00:21:44.700 --> 00:21:47.120
We can't let that
bastard get away!

437
00:21:47.120 --> 00:21:50.410
I'll try to shoot him down!

438
00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:51.660
[USOPP]
Special Attack!

439
00:21:51.660 --> 00:21:55.750
Green Star Platanus Shuriken!

440
00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:01.090
[Kanjuro grunts]

441
00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:02.750
A valiant effort,
but not enough!

442
00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:06.250
I don't have time to
entertain imbeciles like you!

443
00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:09.010
[Sanji grunts]

444
00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:12.840
[Kanjuro cackles]

445
00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:16.810
[grunts]

446
00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:20.020
[SANJI]
What's that cloud?

447
00:22:20.020 --> 00:22:22.930
I have a bad feeling
about this, Sir Sanji!

448
00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:24.480
Turn back, immediately!

449
00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:26.440
[Kanjuro cackling]

450
00:22:26.440 --> 00:22:29.560
Whatever technique he's doing,
I have never seen before!

451
00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:32.400
[KANJURO]
Ink Clouds!

452
00:22:40.470 --> 00:22:41.470
[Samurai gasp]

453
00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:45.890
[gasps]

454
00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:44.390
[groans]

455
00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:50.020
[KANJURO]
Ukiyo Portrait: Evening Shower!

456
00:22:50.020 --> 00:22:55.860
[Samurai screaming]

457
00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:53.370
[Franky grunts]

458
00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:55.370
[Zoro grunts]

459
00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:59.990
It's dangerous here!
Turn the boat around quickly!

460
00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:10.470
Only one man's allowed
to shoot an arrow

461
00:23:10.470 --> 00:23:12.850
through Nami and
Robin's heart, figuratively.

462
00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:15.810
And that man is me!

463
00:23:15.810 --> 00:23:17.400
Sanji!

464
00:23:17.400 --> 00:23:19.730
[cackles]

465
00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:22.780
I am begging you to
please stop this, Kanjuro!

466
00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:26.400
You are going to kill
every last one of them!

467
00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:28.160
That I shall!

468
00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:30.620
And rightfully so.

469
00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:37.250
It's their time!

470
00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:34.560
[All gasp]

471
00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:37.430
[KANJURO]
Your father Oden
and your mother Toki

472
00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:40.270
dangled a false hope
in front of those poor fools

473
00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:42.040
[All gasp]

474
00:23:40.310 --> 00:23:43.020
by delaying their
inevitable deaths.

475
00:23:43.020 --> 00:23:45.230
Now, 20 years later,

476
00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:50.110
their execution must be
completed at last.

477
00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:51.700
Frankly it would be a mercy,

478
00:23:51.700 --> 00:23:54.410
since those foolish samurai
are now serving under

479
00:23:54.410 --> 00:23:57.330
a cowardly little imp
like yourself. Ugh.

480
00:23:57.330 --> 00:24:00.460
You are nothing but an imprudent
child lacking in conviction

481
00:24:00.460 --> 00:24:03.750
and whimpering at
the first sign of danger.

482
00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:08.360
[Kanjuro cackling]

483
00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:06.500
[chuckles]

484
00:24:05.270 --> 00:24:08.360
[Kin'emon grunts] [cackles]

485
00:24:05.860 --> 00:24:08.360
[cries]

486
00:24:08.360 --> 00:24:10.810
[KANJURO]
You can cry, but I will laugh!

487
00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:15.560
What am I to say?

488
00:24:15.560 --> 00:24:19.650
I know, best of all,
that I'm no Kozuki Oden!

489
00:24:19.650 --> 00:24:25.530
For how could I ever
hope to measure up?

490
00:24:26.740 --> 00:24:30.620
[MOMONOSUKE]
What am I
supposed to do? I'm helpless!

491
00:24:30.620 --> 00:24:34.580
[Samurai gasping]

492
00:24:35.960 --> 00:24:38.840
[MOMONOSUKE]
Are you certain
that's what you want to say?

493
00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:44.260
If you tell them that,
no one will come to your aid.

494
00:24:44.260 --> 00:24:45.800
[MOMONOSUKE]
But...

495
00:24:53.540 --> 00:24:58.000
Everyone! Can you hear me?

496
00:24:59.820 --> 00:25:02.240
That's Lord Momonosuke!

497
00:25:02.240 --> 00:25:06.990
[MOMONOSUKE]
I ask you that you
do not worry about my wellbeing!

498
00:25:07.780 --> 00:25:13.040
[MOMONOSUKE]
That is exactly
